chapter 11

Inheritance
- useful for reusing classes that associate with a super class (shape <-- circle, triangle, etc
- "is a" relationship; subclass "is a" superclass

extends keyword
- extends keyword allows subclass to access superclass

Superclass
- superclass, parent class, base class, supertype (same thing, diff names)
- **Can** be inherited by multiple classes

Subclass
- subclass, child(ren) class(es), extended class, derived class, subtype (same thing diff names)
- A subclass inherits all data members, methods (*excluding constructors*) and any changes from a superclass
- The subclass must implement their own constructors, and to access data members from superclass, they must use get/set methods
- A subclass add data and methods and they can override methods
- A subclass **cannot** inherit multiple classes

super keyword
- super. --> superclass
	- method must exist in superclass to use
- super() --> superclass constructor
	- checks signature and matches appropriate method in superclass
- java automatically calls super in child class constructors; given for free


Constructor chaining
- Java executes **all** default superclass constructors up the "extends" chain 
	- Dog() --> Animal() --> Object()

Overriding methods
- Subclasses can override methods from a superclass to uniquely modify a method more suited for the subclass
- an overrided method **must** match the superclass method signature
- private and static methods are not applicable here as they are not modifiable or private
	- **a subclass can still inherit and access a static method using SuperClass.staticMethod()
- Animal toString() can override Object toString to avoid getting the hashcode in a test class